    "plain": "ZEPLIN-III's first run saw no dark matter and showed that two-phase xenon separates signal from background very well at low energy.",
    "technical": "12 kg two-phase xenon TPC; data from 27 Feb - 20 May 2008; WIMP-nucleon spin-independent limit 8.1e-8 pb at 55 GeV/c^2 (90% CL); the abstract states better low-energy discrimination between electron and nuclear recoils than previously achieved by other xenon-based experiments."
